  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "d5ee6a1f-b49a-4450-b511-3aa850625559",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        320,
        -400
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 716,
        "height": 1320,
        "content": "# Read Amazon invoices with AI and log them to Google Sheets\n\nTakes a sheet of Amazon invoice links, opens each one in a cloud browser, screenshots it, files the image in a dated Google Drive folder, and uses AI to read the company, invoice number, date, taxes and total into a spreadsheet row. Built as the follow-up to a workflow that collects the invoice links.\n\n### How it works\n1. A nightly schedule reads the invoice links from your sheet and keeps only rows dated today.\n2. Each invoice is handled one at a time. Airtop opens a cloud browser on the invoice page, zooms out so the whole invoice fits, and takes a screenshot.\n3. The screenshot is uploaded into the current month's folder in Google Drive, then downloaded back so both the file and its shareable links travel together.\n4. One AI agent reads the image, a second turns that reading into strict JSON, and an auto-fixing parser retries if the format is wrong.\n5. The extracted fields are appended to a monthly tab in your spreadsheet and the browser session is closed.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add your Airtop, OpenAI, Google Sheets and Google Drive credentials to the placeholder nodes.\n2. Point the two Google Sheets nodes at your own spreadsheet. The source tab needs an Invoice URL and Date column.\n3. In Google Drive, create folders named by month, for example 2026-04, and select your drive on the Find this month folder node.\n4. In Airtop, create a browser profile, log into Amazon inside it once, and put the profile name in the Start browser session node.\n\n### Customization\nEdit the field list in the two AI agent prompts and the output parser to capture different invoice fields."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
